    {
      "id": "thi-ap5",
      "findings": [
        "Publisher Tīṇinaḷamālikā versus VRI Naḷamālikā is explained by publisher note1 BJTS omission; preserve both labels.",
        "Local3/global39-40 compresses VRI39 and includes first two feet of VRI40; note4 owns its alternative intention, resolve and kinnarī-body wording.",
        "Local4/global40 contains remaining four feet of VRI40, not another whole VRI40; note5 preserves PTS/BJTS mental-act alternatives.",
        "Local5/global42 concerns destroyed/slain existence and corresponds substantively to VRI41; note6 owns reading alternative.",
        "Local6/global41 corresponds substantively to VRI42; source calls the result Buddha-pūjā where VRI main names flower worship. Note7 belongs to local5 and documents BJTS reversal of locals5/6; do not swap text.",
        "Note2 cross-reference to Therāpadāna1886 and note3 lexical explanation remain translator apparatus, not additional canonical text.",
        "Publisher expansion of abbreviated43–45 must not expand the VRI root."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "thi-ap10",
      "findings": [
        "Source122 local7 bad road differs from VRI main dumagge/tree-top; no VRI variant legitimizes silent reconciliation.",
        "Source127 local12 general karma differs from VRI explicit giving water; preserve source wording.",
        "Notes6/7 select BJTS/PTS alternate readings that agree with the VRI main in119/125; keep all alternatives and translator explanations in note apparatus.",
        "Note4 Vipassi identification is an explicit translator inference, not a claim proven by root117.",
        "Note3 Vinaya/Jātaka/Therāpadāna lexical cross-references do not activate or quote those additional texts.",
        "The source chapter summary totals118 while VRI main totals130; VRI6935 contains seventeen/eighteen additional-count variants. Preserve all forms and do not infer missing scripture.",
